      "title": "Quality / resolution / validation",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Quality baseline\nNative canvas: **768 x 1344**. 124 frames at 24 fps is **5.167 seconds**, not exactly 5 seconds. Other valid lengths: 141, 158, 175, 192, 209, 226, 243, 260, 277, 294, 311, 328, 345, 362.\n\nReference `max` keeps up to a 2048-pixel short edge and does not upscale small references. It is slower and uses more memory. The native 768 x 1344 canvas is approximately 1 MP; arbitrary 2K/4K diffusion is not a validated quality upgrade. Add Guide cover-crops to the canvas, so preview endpoint framing before an expensive run.\n\nFull BF16 weights, native VAEs, no added turbo LoRA, no sparse attention, no face restoration. H3 launch uses dense PyTorch attention.\n\n30 steps is a starting point, not a measured optimum. Compare 40 or 50 with the SAME seed and inputs only after the baseline looks right. `beta` / `normal` are optional scheduler A/B tests, not guarantees of improvement.\n\nSource-pinned build. Offline graph and media checks only; Docker, real ComfyUI import and GPU quality still require live validation. Only your SAM local-edit workflow retains approved status."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
